  "exact_proof_route": [
    "Bundle the literal actual W using public Regularity smoothness and compact support; no assumed target derivative or Fourier estimate.",
    "Native directional words evaluated on unit Euclidean basis vectors are controlled by the actual Frechet norm. Delta has d words of order2; Delta squared has d squared words of order4. The word order is retained without invoking mixed-partial commutation.",
    "Actual normalizedFourth equals (f-tau Delta f)-tau(Delta f-tau Delta squared f), tau=((2pi)^2)^(-1). Triangle and native linearity yield norm at most (1+tau*d)^2 times a common0/2/4 derivative bound.",
    "Native iterated word support inclusion shows normalizedFourth vanishes outside tsupport f and hence outside fixed K=tsupport Q.",
    "Set integral equals full integral because of actual pointwise zero on the complement. Native finite compact volume and norm_setIntegral_le_of_norm_le_const give integral norm(A)^2 <= B^2*volume.real K. Native sqrt monotonicity/product/square give L2 energy root <=B*sqrt(volume.real K). No energy bound is assumed.",
    "Choose real Mixed C4>0 for J4 before all Z,u0,rho0,R. Set p=1+R>=1, all jets0..4 <=C4*p^4. Apply generic genuine fourier_integral_norm_le_normalizedFourth at finrank=d<8 and combine. Final witness is1+Cd*((1+tau*d)^2*C4)*sqrt(volume.real(tsupport Q))."
  ],
